// pendingApprovalCard renders one PendingApprovalCard -- board 07's own grid card. A plain
// navigation to the step's own detail page (2026-09-19: dropped the hx-get/hx-target inline swap
// this used to layer on top -- a worklist click opens the record's page, not a pane below).
//
// The card became a <div> wrapping an inner <a> (2026-09-25, Flow 2 gap study Tahap 4), rather than
// the whole card staying one <a>: a Rejected row's own Revise button (below) is a second
// interactive element, and a <form>/<button> nested inside an <a> is invalid HTML that browsers
// handle inconsistently on click. Every other status still behaves identically -- the inner <a>
// wraps the same content this templ always rendered, and the hover style moved to the outer <div>
// with it.
//
// Page-internal on purpose: capabilities.md records it as cataloged-but-not-yet-reused, which is
// the honest state until a second, genuinely different screen needs the identical shape.
// slaPillTone is the urgent SLA pill's colour (owner decision S1, 2026-10-12): overdue reads the `bad` tone and due
// today reads `warn`, so theme.tone moves both. Before, due today was a literal amber-700, one step lighter than the
// warn ink (amber-800); the Design System had already folded amber ink to `tone-warn-ink`. Chosen in Go so the two
// states cannot collide as templ.KV keys (L12).
func slaPillTone(ctx context.Context, overdue bool) string {
	if overdue {
		return toneClass(ctx, domain.ToneBad)
	}
	return toneClass(ctx, domain.ToneWarn)
}

// approvalCardEdge is the card's edge for its state, chosen in Go. It was moved out of two templ.KV keys because a
// Workspace mapping `bad` to the grey palette made the overdue edge and the surface edge one string, and templ
// dropped it (L12). Since DS-D15 stage 2 every role has its own class, so that collision cannot recur; choosing in Go
// stays the plainer shape, and the shape gates read this helper (stateEdgeHelperCall).
func approvalCardEdge(ctx context.Context, overdue bool) string {
	if overdue {
		return toneEdgeClass(ctx, domain.ToneBad)
	}
	return borderClass(ctx, domain.BorderSurface)
}

